/F1 9.5 Tf
(Q3: State Newton's second law of motion.) Tj
/F1 9 Tf
0 -13 Td
(Ans: The force acting on a body is directly proportional to the rate of change of linear momentum of the body and the change in momentum takes place in the direction of the force. Formula: F = ma. [2 Marks]) Tj
0 -13 Td
0 -8 Td
/F1 9.5 Tf
(Q4: Differentiate between Mass and Weight.) Tj
/F1 9 Tf
0 -13 Td
(Ans: 1\) Mass: Fundamental quantity, scalar, measured in kg, remains constant everywhere. [1 Mark]) Tj
0 -13 Td
(     2\) Weight: Derived quantity, vector, measured in Newton \(N\), varies with acceleration due to gravity \(W = mg\). [1 Mark]) Tj
0 -12 Td
0 -8 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(### 7 Marks Comprehensive Board Question) Tj
/F1 9 Tf
0 -15 Td
/F1 9.5 Tf
(Q5: State and prove the Law of Conservation of Linear Momentum.) Tj
/F1 9 Tf
0 -13 Td
(Ans: Statement: In the absence of an external force, the total linear momentum of a system of bodies remains constant. [1 Mark]) Tj
0 -13 Td
(Step 1: Setup: Let two bodies A and B of masses m1 and m2 move with initial velocities u1 and u2 \(u1 > u2\). [1 Mark]) Tj
0 -12 Td
(Step 2: Force during collision: Body A exerts action force F_B on B, and B exerts reaction force F_A on A. [1 Mark]) Tj
0 -12 Td
(Step 3: By Newton's Second Law: F_B = m2\(v2 - u2\)/t and F_A = m1\(v1 - u1\)/t. [1 Mark]) Tj
0 -12 Td
(Step 4: By Newton's Third Law: Action = -Reaction => F_B = -F_A. [1 Mark]) Tj
0 -12 Td
(Step 5: Equating equations: m2\(v2 - u2\)/t = -m1\(v1 - u1\)/t => m2 v2 - m2 u2 = -m1 v1 + m1 u1. [1 Mark]) Tj
0 -12 Td
(Step 6: Final Result: m1 u1 + m2 u2 = m1 v1 + m2 v2. Total initial momentum = Total final momentum. Hence proved. [1 Mark]) Tj
0 -12 Td
